Modifications
-------------
Cubiq Launcher is a modified version of TRS Launcher. On 2026-10-27 PwiePixel made these changes
(the full list is in the Git history of this repository):
- New name (Cubiq Launcher, Cubiq Client), own logo, app icons and start animation.
- New launcher design: a clean, dark look in the green of the Cubiq logo instead of the redstone
  look; the launcher's extra designs of the original (winter, fox) were removed.
- New identifiers and namespaces (app id dev.pwiepixel.cubiqlauncher, Java/Kotlin packages
  dev.pwiepixel.*, mod id cubiqclient, data folder Cubiq-Launcher, cubiq-launcher:// links).
- Online services, Microsoft sign-in and Discord status are switched off until this build is given
  its own server, Azure app and Discord app; no data is sent to the services of the original.
- Version numbering restarted at 0.1.0.
Files that carry the original copyright header keep it.

Cubiq Launcher is not affiliated with or endorsed by the TRS Launcher project or its author.

Third-party parts
-----------------
- Polyfrost OneLauncher (GPL-3.0-only): parts of the launcher's process handling are adapted from
  https://github.com/Polyfrost/OneLauncher
- Chat Heads by dzwdz (MPL-2.0): parts of the Cubiq Client chat heads code (client-mod, packages
  "chatheads") are based on https://github.com/dzwdz/chat_heads. Those files keep their MPL-2.0
  header; the license text is in client-mod/licenses/chat-heads-MPL-2.0.txt.
- AppleSkin by squeek502 (The Unlicense): idea for the Cubiq Client hunger overlay; resource packs
  that ship AppleSkin textures are supported.
- Inter by Rasmus Andersson (SIL Open Font License 1.1, via @fontsource-variable/inter): the
  launcher's font.
- Fonts for the Halloween look (SIL Open Font License 1.1, bundled in app/assets/fonts with their
  license texts): IM Fell English SC by Igino Marini; Cormorant Garamond by The Cormorant Project
  Authors (Christian Thalmann).
- Mobile game engine (src-tauri/plugins/tauri-plugin-cubiq-game, Android; details and pinned
  commits/hashes in android/vendor/*/UPSTREAM.md and android/prebuilt.lock):
  - Amethyst-Android by AngelAuraMC, a fork of PojavLauncher by PojavLauncherTeam
    (LGPL-3.0-or-later): JNI engine (JVM launcher, EGL/GL bridge, GLFW input bridge, exit and
    dlopen hooks), Android glue classes and the GLFW stub for LWJGL 3.3.3/3.4.1 – vendored in
    android/vendor/amethyst (license in that folder). jre_launcher.c contains code from OpenJDK
    (GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception, Oracle).
  - androidnsbypass by alexytomi (MIT), partly based on liblinkernsbypass by Billy Laws
    (BSD-2-Clause) – vendored in android/vendor/androidnsbypass.
  - Downloaded at build time (SHA-256 pinned, not in the repository): MobileGlues by MobileGL-Dev
    (LGPL-2.1), NG-GL4ES / Krypton Wrapper by BZLZHH (MIT, based on gl4es by ptitSeb, MIT),
    OpenAL Soft (LGPL-2.0-or-later), LWJGL 3 and its Android fork by PojavLauncherTeam
    (BSD-3-Clause) with FreeType (FreeType License), JSR-305 annotations (BSD-3-Clause),
    bytehook by ByteDance (MIT), JNA (Apache-2.0 / LGPL-2.1), SDL3 by the SDL developers (zlib;
    Android build from Amethyst-Android), SPIRV-Cross by Khronos/Arm (Apache-2.0) and shaderc by
    Google (Apache-2.0, part of the LWJGL 3.4.1 Android natives).
  - The SDL3 Android Java glue (org.libsdl.app, zlib, with Amethyst-Android changes, LGPL-3.0-or-later)
    is vendored in android/vendor/amethyst/java/org/libsdl/app.
  - Downloaded at runtime (SHA-256 pinned, never bundled): OpenJDK 8/17/21/25 runtimes for
    Android built by AngelAuraMC (angelauramc-openjdk-build), GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception.
- Amethyst-iOS by Tran Hoang Khanh Duy and the PojavLauncher/Amethyst contributors (GPL-3.0):
  the iOS game engine (JVM start, GL/EGL and input bridge, JIT detection and dyld helpers) is based
  on https://github.com/AngelAuraMC/Amethyst-iOS at commit 9212a1894865e7ac0466029e25ddb0d895544c76.
  Vendored files, local patches and the parts taken at build time are listed in
  src-tauri/plugins/tauri-plugin-cubiq-game/ios/Engine/vendor/amethyst-ios/UPSTREAM.md. The iOS app
  additionally ships, unchanged from that commit: MobileGlues (LGPL-2.1), ANGLE (BSD-3-Clause),
  gl4es (MIT), Mesa OSMesa (MIT), MoltenVK (Apache-2.0), LWJGL (BSD-3-Clause), OpenAL Soft
  (LGPL-2.0), FreeType (FTL), shaderc (Apache-2.0), Caciocavallo (GPL-2.0 with Classpath
  Exception), fishhook (BSD-3-Clause), Gson (Apache-2.0). Java runtimes (OpenJDK, GPL-2.0 with
  Classpath Exception) are downloaded by the app at runtime and are not part of it.
- e4mc by Skye (MIT, https://github.com/vgskye/e4mc-minecraft-architectury): the "public link" for local
  servers in the launcher speaks e4mc's quiclime protocol (own Rust implementation over quinn) and uses e4mc's
  public broker and relays (*.e4mc.link). The Cubiq Client's e4mc bridge ships the e4mc MIT licence text.
- Further libraries and bundled mods are listed with their licenses in README.md and
  client-mod/README.md.

